{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin the movie explores the founding of facebook and the legal battles that followed it the film is a fascinating exploration of ambition, power, and the cost of success\n\nthe social network stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the ceo and founder of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, the co-founder of the company eisenberg delivers a standout performance as the brilliant and ambitious zuckerberg, who is driven to create a social networking site that will change the world\n\nthe film opens with zuckerberg creating a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the faces of two female students and vote on which one is more attractive the site quickly becomes popular, but it also attracts the attention of the university administration, who accuse zuckerberg of violating privacy laws\n\nzuckerberg then teams up with saverin to create thefacebook, a social networking site that is initially limited to students at harvard university the site quickly gains popularity, and zuckerberg and saverin decide to expand it to other colleges and universities\n\nhowever, the partnership between zuckerberg and saverin begins to deteriorate as zuckerberg becomes more and more obsessed with the success of thefacebook and less interested in sharing the profits with saverin the two men eventually have a falling out, and saverin files a lawsuit against zuckerberg\n\nthe social network also explores the legal battle between zuckerberg and the winklevoss twins, harvard classmates who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea for a social networking site called connectU zuckerberg denies the accusations, but the winklevoss twins sue him for theft of intellectual property\n\nthroughout the film, fincher and sorkin explore the themes of ambition, power, and the cost of success zuckerberg is portrayed as a brilliant and ambitious young man who is willing to do whatever it takes to achieve his goals, even if it means betraying his friends and partners\n\nthe film also raises questions about the nature of innovation and the role of technology in our lives thefacebook, and later facebook, has had a profound impact on the way we communicate and interact with each other, but it has also raised concerns about privacy and the ethical implications of social media\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted and thought-provoking film that offers a fascinating look at the early days of facebook and the legal battles that followed it the film is anchored by strong performances from eisenberg, garfield, and the rest of the cast, and it is a must-see for anyone interested in the intersection of technology, power, and human nature.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.002708934945985675}, {"token": "social", "logprob": -3.3378546504536644e-06}, {"token": "network", "logprob": -2.8371408916427754e-05}, {"token": "is", "logprob": -1.9430925021879375e-05}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -3.3378546504536644e-06}, {"token": "", "logprob": -1.583573818206787}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "film", "logprob": -0.2529076337814331}, {"token": "directed", "logprob": -0.004620945546776056}, {"token": "by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "d", "logprob": -0.00023195437097456306}, {"token": "avid", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "fin", "logprob": -0.0031316070817410946}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.01943988911807537}, {"token": "written", "logprob": -6.341733387671411e-05}, {"token": "by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.0001532914029667154}, {"token": "aron", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "s", "logprob": -0.000277123210253194}, {"token": "ork", "logprob": -8.654219709569588